MCTAL probe: how multi-level tally bins expand
c Slab 3 (x 0..20, y -10..10) is filled with a 2 x 2 lattice of 10 cm
c elements (indices 0:1 in x and y; one more around, only so that a ray on
c an element boundary finds one), each holding box 8 in cell 9. The values
c are not the point (one ray along +x through y = 0.3); the bins MCNP makes
c are: the output file names them, MCTAL counts them. (A union of whole
c chains, ((8 < 7[0 0 0] < 3) (9 < 3)), is a fatal error.)
c Regenerate with: mcnp6 i=levels.mcnp n=levels.
1 0  10 -11 15 -16 17 -18 imp:n=1
2 0  11 -12 15 -16 17 -18 imp:n=1
3 0  12 -13 15 -16 17 -18 imp:n=1 fill=1
4 0  13 -14 15 -16 17 -18 imp:n=1
5 0  -99 #1 #2 #3 #4 imp:n=1
6 0  99 imp:n=0
7 0  -22 21 -24 23 -26 25 imp:n=1 u=1 lat=1 fill=-1:2 -1:2 0:0 2 15r
8 0  30 -31 32 -33 34 -35 imp:n=1 u=2
9 0  #8 imp:n=1 u=2

10 PX -40
11 PX -20
12 PX 0
13 PX 20
14 PX 40
15 PY -10
16 PY 10
17 PZ -10
18 PZ 10
21 PX 0
22 PX 10
23 PY -10
24 PY 0
25 PZ -10
26 PZ 10
30 PX 2
31 PX 8
32 PY -8
33 PY -2
34 PZ -5
35 PZ 5
99 SO 200

MODE N
SDEF POS=-100 0.3 0.7 VEC=1 0 0 DIR=1 ERG=14 TME=0
NPS 10
PRDMP 2j 1
VOL 8000 8000 8000 8000 1 1 2000 360 1640
FC4 union at the first level
F4:N ((8 9) < 3)
FC14 a lattice element in parentheses
F14:N (8 < (7[0:1 0:0 0:0]) < 3)
FC24 two cells over a 2 x 2 range
F24:N (8 9 < 7[0:1 0:1 0:0] < 3)
FC34 a 2 x 2 range and the T bin
F34:N (8 < 7[0:1 0:1 0:0] < 3) T
FC44 listed elements, then another chain
F44:N (8 < 7[0 0 0] 7[1 1 0] < 3) (9 < 3)
FC54 the lattice cell with no index
F54:N (8 < 7 < 3)
FC64 the last level in parentheses
F64:N (8 < 7[0:1 0:1 0:0] < (3))
FC84 several first-level cells, then a single chain, then T
F84:N (8 9 < 7[0 0 0] < 3) (8 < 7[1 0 0] < 3) T
FC94 plain cells and a group with T
F94:N 1 (2 4) T
